% Background theory: pairwise distinctness, declared by the parties.
%
% No two of the names below denote one measure.  Neither module
% asserts this, so the rule is the parties' and a verdict resting
% on an instance of it is withdrawable by abandoning the rule.
%
% Distinctness, not disjointness: a measure may lie below another
% and still be a different measure, and a use employing two of
% them is not claiming they are one.  Disjointness over a pair
% with a common child would contradict the resource.
%
% The rule is stated here and instantiated by the problems.  A
% problem naming two of the measures below carries the inequation
% between them as a bg_dist_ assertion, so that a refutation cites
% the instance it used rather than one of 2701.
%
% Measures: 74
% Pairs   : 2701
%
% tm_access_control_method, tm_activity_monitoring, tm_anonymisation, tm_asymmetric_cryptography, tm_asymmetric_encryption, tm_authentication_a_b_c
% tm_authentication_p_a_b_c, tm_authentication_protocols, tm_authorisation_protocols, tm_biometric_authentication, tm_cryptographic_authentication, tm_cryptographic_key_management
